// Bandit Level 26 → Level 27

URL: https://overthewire.org/wargames/bandit/

Step1: We already have the SSH key from the previous level.

        bandit26.sshkey

Step2: Make the terminal very small and connect as `bandit26`:

        ssh -i /tmp/bandit26.sshkey bandit26@bandit.labs.overthewire.org -p 2220

Step3: Because the shell uses `more`, press:

        v

Step4: This opens the file in `vim`.

Step5: Set the shell to Bash:

        :set shell=/bin/bash

Step6: Start the Bash shell:

        :shell

Step7: We now have a shell as `bandit26`.

Step8: List the files:

        ls

Step9: We can see:

        bandit27-do
        text.txt

Step10: Check what `bandit27-do` does:

        ./bandit27-do

Step11: It says:

        Run a command as another user.
        Example: ./bandit27-do id

Step12: The binary is a SUID executable owned by `bandit27`, so it can execute commands with `bandit27` privileges.

Step13: Use it to read the Bandit Level 27 password:

        ./bandit27-do cat /etc/bandit_pass/bandit27

Step14: The password for Bandit Level 27 is:

        3ba3118a22e93127a4ed485be72ef5ea

Step15: The Bandit Level 26 → Level 27 challenge is solved.

